SWEET AMP (patch 0158, plan 2026-11-14 oneshot-2 step A7), boot-arg sweetamp=1: the two CS35L41 speaker amps of oriole (USI13 / SPI13). Inert unless
sweetamp=1 AND the ADT root model-number is "oriole". One synchronous run from sweet_ufs_init, before the touch / battery threads: the A1 identify
(the port of the shim --amp-id, pk-amp shim/ampid.c 4c7be85, review SAFE round 2; A1 PASS on hardware o5-a1-ampid) and, on each amp that identified as CS35L41 B2 with OTP_BOOT_DONE, the
stock probe-time writes: IRQ1_MASK1 = INT1_MASK_DEFAULT, the B2 errata patch, DSP1_CCM_CORE_CTRL = 0 (cs35l41.c:4306-4308, :3675-3686, :4351-4362,
:4401). cs35l41_otp_unpack is NOT done (its bit maps are GPL data tables, cs35l41-tables.c: not copied; blocked). The write allowlist is exactly those
12 (register, value) pairs; PWR_CTRL1 / GLOBAL_EN is never written (refused by name). IRQ1_STATUS1 error bits (seven) must be 0 before the first write and after the writes, then both resets go
low and every pad / controller / sysreg / mux word is restored and read back. Lines "SWEET AMP: ..."; pass "SWEET AMP: init ok (no otp unpack) l,r devid 35a40
rev b2, errors=0" (A7 PARTIAL), then "SWEET AMP: verdict PASS". Host test shim/amp_xnu_host_test.c (header extracted from this patch). BUILT, UNRUN; needs A1 PASS and an independent review first.

